WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.458
Carefully, Vinnie and Mandy moved closer to the ship being tied to the dock.

2
00:00:06.459 --> 00:00:12.073
The Redcoat captain was speaking to a tall man in a black hat.

3
00:00:12.074 --> 00:00:20.244
He wore a long coat, pants that ended just below his knees, white stockings, and black shoes.

4
00:00:20.245 --> 00:00:32.346
"Mr. John Hancock," the captain read from a paper, "by order of His Royal Highness, King George III of England, you are under arrest."

5
00:00:32.347 --> 00:00:36.978
"What have I done?" John Hancock asked calmly.

6
00:00:36.979 --> 00:00:44.948
"Your ship, The Liberty , is carrying illegal tea into Boston Harbor," said the

7
00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:50.696
captain. Before John Hancock could say anything, the soldiers took him

8
00:00:50.697 --> 00:00:54.030
away. The men on the dock followed

9
00:00:54.031 --> 00:00:59.517
angrily. One of them saw Vinnie and Mandy and quickly walked

10
00:00:59.518 --> 00:01:04.101
over. "What are your names?" he asked when he got

11
00:01:04.102 --> 00:01:09.833
close. "I’m Vinnie, and this is my sister Mandy," said Vinnie

12
00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:14.066
bravely. "Are you American patriots?" the man

13
00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:17.599
asked. "Yes, sir!" Vinnie said

14
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.279
proudly. "Good," the man

15
00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.602
said. He took out a piece of paper and wrote something on

16
00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:28.470
it. "You must find John Adams and give this to

17
00:01:28.471 --> 00:01:32.766
him. Go quickly. No one will suspect

18
00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:37.721
you." "Yes, sir." Vinnie saluted, but the man didn’t

19
00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:41.858
see. He had already moved away to rejoin the

20
00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:46.869
others. "Vinnie! Why did you say that?" Mandy

21
00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.440
said. "We don’t even know who those men

22
00:01:50.441 --> 00:01:54.968
are!" "John Hancock? John Adams? Come on,

23
00:01:54.969 --> 00:01:57.152
Mandy. We are in

24
00:01:57.153 --> 00:02:02.273
Boston. These are the founders of our country!" Vinnie said passionately.

25
00:02:02.274 --> 00:02:06.142
"Right now, America is under British rule.

26
00:02:06.143 --> 00:02:08.507
We must help."

27
00:02:08.508 --> 00:02:12.361
"So what can we do?" she asked.

28
00:02:12.362 --> 00:02:19.290
"Just as the man said, we must find John Adams," explained Vinnie.

29
00:02:19.291 --> 00:02:23.694
The children walked down the busy Boston streets.

30
00:02:23.695 --> 00:02:28.312
Horses, carriages, and wagons were everywhere.

31
00:02:28.313 --> 00:02:31.768
Women were in simple cotton dresses.

32
00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:34.746
Men wore three-cornered hats.

33
00:02:34.747 --> 00:02:41.750
As they approached an intersection, Vinnie and Mandy heard shouting and clapping.

34
00:02:41.751 --> 00:02:45.563
"What’s going on?" Vinnie wondered.

35
00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:51.913
On the next street, a crowd was gathered in front of a man standing on a barrel.

36
00:02:51.914 --> 00:02:54.798
He looked excited and angry.

37
00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:59.639
"Should we pay taxes to the British?" he shouted.

38
00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.929
"No!" the crowd cheered.

39
00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.570
"We have no vote!

40
00:03:06.571 --> 00:03:11.680
We have no one to speak for us in England!" the man continued.

41
00:03:11.681 --> 00:03:14.661
People shouted loudly.

42
00:03:14.662 --> 00:03:18.067
"The Redcoats take over our homes!

43
00:03:18.068 --> 00:03:21.401
We pay too much for our tea!

44
00:03:21.402 --> 00:03:26.917
We even pay too much to mail our letters!" cried the man.

45
00:03:26.918 --> 00:03:32.325
"Who is he?" Mandy asked a boy standing nearby.

46
00:03:32.326 --> 00:03:36.615
"That’s Mr. Keith, the grocer," said the boy.

47
00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:40.135
"Why is he shouting?" asked Vinnie.

48
00:03:40.136 --> 00:03:42.812
The boy stared at them.

49
00:03:42.813 --> 00:03:47.198
"You aren’t from Boston, are you?" he said.

50
00:03:47.199 --> 00:03:50.328
"King George signed the Stamp Act.

51
00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:55.746
The law makes us pay extra money, a tax, for everything we buy.

52
00:03:55.747 --> 00:03:59.238
Everyone is very angry about it."

53
00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:10.856
"I never knew America was like this once," Mandy whispered to Vinnie.

